From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dmayala <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:55:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0058z] drm/a9_eink: read the vblank count under t->lock
 (review 89e C2)

a9x_vblank() read t->vbl_ref and t->ms->crtc without the transport lock;
a9x_free_locked() (msm unbind) clears t->ms before vbl_ref under that lock,
so a settle racing an unbind could dereference a NULL or freed modeset.
Take t->lock and check t->ms. The settle loop holds no transport lock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/a9_eink/a9_eink_transport.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/a9_eink/a9_eink_transport.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/a9_eink/a9_eink_transport.c
index c704f644a..209468939 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/a9_eink/a9_eink_transport.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/a9_eink/a9_eink_transport.c
@@ -722,16 +722,21 @@ int a9x_power_on(struct a9x_transport *t)
 
 /*
  * F6b (review 89d): the scanout's vblank count and time, for the PG settle
- * trace. Read-only and lockless: while the transport is on it holds a vblank
- * reference (vbl_ref), so the count is live; 0 otherwise.
+ * trace. Read-only. Under t->lock (review 89e C2): a9x_free_locked() clears
+ * t->ms and vbl_ref under the same lock when msm unbinds, so the modeset is
+ * never used after it is freed. The callers (the settle loop, worker thread)
+ * hold no transport lock and no lock that nests inside t->lock. 0 when no
+ * vblank reference is held or the modeset is gone.
  */
 u64 a9x_vblank(struct a9x_transport *t, s64 *at_us)
 {
 	ktime_t kt = 0;
 	u64 n = 0;
 
-	if (READ_ONCE(t->vbl_ref))
+	mutex_lock(&t->lock);
+	if (t->vbl_ref && t->ms)
 		n = drm_crtc_vblank_count_and_time(t->ms->crtc, &kt);
+	mutex_unlock(&t->lock);
 	*at_us = ktime_to_us(kt);
 	return n;
 }
